  "caveat": "The official Java 1.21.x BuiltinFauna data provider contains habitat constraints for all 78 registered fauna. These include temperature, groundwater (or average rainfall when ignoreRivers=true), forest density, seasonal months, depth, brightness and spawn chance. All 78 also have source-derived placement types. The older v3.2.26 fauna JSON baseline contains 63 climate profiles and is retained separately for provenance comparison. Bedrock's environment sampler does not yet supply all required TFC inputs (notably groundwater, rain variance and hemispheric month), so source-complete data must not be mistaken for runtime-complete natural spawning. The legacy 63-species implementation remains runtime tracked; species-specific AI, diet, breeding, products, drops, genetics and in-game validation remain incomplete.",
